<article class="information-page">
    <h1>My Teaching Philosophy</h1>
    <p>To me, the purpose of early childhood education is self-discovery and helping children make sense of the world around them. Life is about learning, and young children learn best when they feel safe, valued, and connected.</p>
    <p>At Miss Mary’s Little Lambs, I prioritize belonging above all else. I want every child to feel seen, heard, and accepted for who they are. When children feel like they matter and truly belong, they develop the confidence to explore, take risks, and grow.</p>
    <p>I approach teaching with a nurturing mindset, always pausing to connect with children first when they are struggling emotionally, behaviorally, or academically. I believe relationships are the foundation for all learning and development.</p>
    <p>Children learn best through a variety of experiences, including demonstration, hands-on exploration, conversation, and collaboration with their peers. I design learning experiences that allow children to engage actively with materials, ideas, and one another, supporting both independence and social growth.</p>
    <p>My role as an educator is to guide, support, and create a classroom environment where curiosity is encouraged and learning feels meaningful and joyful. I strive to help children not only build early academic skills, but also develop confidence, empathy, and a sense of wonder about the world.</p>
</article>
